# AGENTS.md — `reporting/` (papers, posters, slides, writeups)

Root `../AGENTS.md` applies. Human orientation: [`README.md`](README.md). This is
human-authored, human-owned writing — agents assist, they don't author.

## You may
- Draft and revise prose *for the user to review* (intro scaffolding, methods from
  the actual pipeline, figure legends).
- Wire figure references to `../results/figures/light/` (papers/posters/writeups) or
  `../results/figures/dark/` (dark slides).
- Fix LaTeX/Markdown build errors; keep `_assets/refs.bib` tidy.
- Build paper/poster/writeup PDFs with the shared `_assets/lab.cls`; the Beamer
  deck uses its own class and shares only `_assets/fonts.tex` + the theme colours.

## You may not (without the user)
- **Finalize or commit manuscript / abstract / grant text.** A human owns the
  words. Draft, then hand off.
- **Fabricate results, numbers, or citations.** Every figure must point at a real
  build target in `results/`; every citation must be a real entry the user added.
  If a number isn't in `results/`, don't write it.
- **Edit `_assets/theme-colors.tex`.** It is generated from `../conf/theme/` — change
  the theme source, not the generated file.

## Conventions to honor
- Reference figures; don't copy them — **except** in `papers/*/submissions/`, where
  freezing (copying the exact PDF + figures) is required.
- Record the results git SHA / {{ data_versioning }} rev an artifact was built from.
- Dated/point-in-time artifacts (decks, submissions) are not edited in place — make
  a new one.
